# Snapshot payloads are not committed. Their sha256 hashes are in
# data/manifest.json, which is committed, so a re-download can be verified
# byte for byte without carrying ~180 MB of data in git history.
data/raw/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# The hand-off artefact is uploaded to the room by hash, not carried in git:
# it is a 1 MB derivative of payload that is itself not committed, and the
# labellers fetch it from the vault. draw.json and the two id lists ARE
# committed, because the draw must be checkable from the repository alone.
data/sample/handoff-150.json

# Pipeline output goes to the room as an artefact by hash, like the hand-off.
# The parameters and the code are committed; the scores are not, because
# registration section 4 keeps the labellers blind to them.
# development-50-v1.json is NOT ignored, and it is the third file to teach this
# lesson today. metrics.py reads it to recompute the figures published at
# cordis-sdg seq 129 before it reports anything new, so a clone without it
# cannot run the reproduction block's metrics line at all — verified by cloning
# and watching it fail. It is 100 KB and it is EVIDENCE rather than output: the
# self-proof is only checkable by someone else if the thing it checks against is
# in the repository.
data/pipeline/development-50-explanations-v1.json
data/pipeline/development-50-explanations-v2.json
data/pipeline/evaluation-100-v2.json
data/pipeline/development-50-v2.json
data/pipeline/dev50-adjudication-v2.json
data/sample/handoff-evaluation-100.json

# NOT ignored, and the reason is the same one that applies to data/corpus/
# figures.json: THE NOTEBOOK READS IT. data/pipeline/evaluation-100-metrics.json
# is 15 KB and is one of the notebook's three inputs, so a clone without it
# cannot re-execute the notebook — which is exactly what happened, verified by
# cloning and watching nbconvert fail on the first cell. Counsel found the
# consequence at cordis-sdg seq 267 from the other side: the file was missing
# from another seat's clone too.

# The section 4.7 metrics report, like the other pipeline output: posted to the
# room as an artefact by hash. metrics.py and the label artefacts it reads are
# committed, so the report is reproducible from the repository.

# The corpus records and the section 6 mapping table: 146 MB of hand-off-shaped
# records and the table built from them. Both are derivatives of payload that is
# itself not committed, and both go to the room as artefacts by hash.
# The contents rather than the directory: git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT is excluded, so "data/corpus/" plus a negation silently does nothing.
data/corpus/*
# …except the figure counts. 90 KB, what the notebook plots, and the notebook
# cannot be re-executed from the repository without them.
!data/corpus/figures.json
